A||||2||87ECO5||Engine Bay Painting Question||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||03-07-2000||04:10 PM||||When painting surfaces in the engine bay, I know it's recommended to use special paint that's designed to withstand the intense heat in there.  However, if I wanted to use a special color not available in a heat-resistant paint, would I be safe if I applied it as a basecoat between both heat-resistant primer and clearcoat paint?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/paint.jpg"> <P>TIA<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||03-07-2000||06:33 PM||||I think the need for a high temp paint is so the paint itself won't blister from the heat.. putting another coat of paint and clearcoat on top of the high temp paint might be useless.<P>Either way, I'm just planning on painting my engine bay black.. glossy if possible, but flat black is perfectly acceptable. the wheel wells too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||03-07-2000||07:16 PM||||I believe the engine compartment is painted with "semi-flat black" It ain't flat and it ain't glossy. And it ain't semi-glossy either!||||reg||1
